# Data Layer Rule

This rule documents the conventions and responsibilities of the Data Layer in the Mozome Flutter project.

## Scope

- Applies to: `data/` directory and related files.

## Topics

- Repository implementations (CRUD/data logic)
- Data sources: Firestore, REST, GraphQL, Shared Preferences, Remote Config, Database, Cloud Messaging
- Mappers for data transformation
- Data Config: environment-specific configuration
- Dependency injection for data services
- Error handling and functional programming patterns

## Best Practices

- Implement domain contracts
- Handle all external data sources and persistence
- Write unit and integration tests for repositories and data sources
- Use Either<Failure, T> pattern for error handling
- Implement proper caching strategies where appropriate
- Follow mapper pattern for converting DTOs to domain entities

